          "text": "The image is a two-panel educational figure labeled Fig. 4, titled 'PIV cameras and viewing direction (flow from above)'. The left panel is a photograph of PIV camera equipment mounted on a vertical support structure, likely inside a wind tunnel, with visible cabling and dark background walls. The right panel is a schematic diagram showing a circular cross-section with a bold black cross representing horizontal and vertical axes. A green arrow indicates the light sheet or viewing direction, annotated with a 30.65° angle relative to the vertical axis. A dashed line extends from the circle to a camera icon, annotated with a distance of 5.6 m. The diagram illustrates the camera viewing direction relative to the wind tunnel axis.\nPIV 相机 视角方向 风洞 光片 粒子图像测速 实验装置 示意图\nPIV cameras viewing direction wind tunnel light sheet particle image velocimetry experimental setup schematic\nFig. 4. PIV cameras and viewing direction (flow from above)\n30.65°\n5.6m\nThe left photograph shows the physical PIV camera setup, which corresponds to the schematic on the right.\nThe green arrow in the schematic represents the light sheet or viewing direction.\nThe angle 30.65° is measured between the green arrow and the vertical axis of the circular cross-section.\nThe dashed line with distance 5.6 m connects the camera icon to the measurement region.",
