          "text": "The figure is a composite of two black-and-white photographs illustrating flow seeding, corresponding to the caption about seed particle distribution in the settling chamber and test section. The left panel shows the interior of a wind tunnel settling chamber, featuring a rectangular distribution rake made of a grid of horizontal and vertical pipes. A seed stream is visible emanating from the rake, appearing as a bright, hazy plume in the lower right of this panel. Several dark, thin lines cross the view diagonally, likely support wires or cables. The right panel shows a close-up of the seeded flow field in the test section. The image is covered with a speckled pattern of bright seed particles on a dark background. In the center, there is a distinctly darker, circular region with a lower density of seed particles. A white arrow points from the lower left toward this dark region. At the bottom of the right panel, the text 'Tip vortex' is visible in white.\n粒子图像测速 种子粒子 风洞 沉降室 试验段 布撒耙 梢涡 流场显示 示踪粒子 DEHS\nPIV seed particles wind tunnel settling chamber test section distribution rake tip vortex flow visualization tracer particles DEHS\nTip vortex\nThe left panel depicts the distribution rake in the settling chamber.\nThe right panel shows the seed particle distribution in the test section.\nThe white arrow in the right panel points to a dark region labeled 'Tip vortex'.\nThe left and right panels are presented side-by-side to compare the seeding setup and the resulting flow field.",
